 "kicker": "NORDBAY \u00b7 NEW ORLEANS \u00b7 PART 2 OF 2",
 "caption": "PART 2/2 \u2014 53 minutes after the first hit, Nordbay struck New Orleans again. \u26a0\ufe0f\ud83d\udea2\n\nDamaged and still moving, the empty Aframax had to round Algiers Point. Tugs were turned away, the master was on the phone \u2014 and at 23:06 she hit the Mandeville Street Wharf. Total damage: about $6.4 million.\n\nNTSB lessons: a pilot on board never removes the master's duty to navigate safely, and no call is more important than a ship still under way.\n\nWhat would you have done? \ud83d\udc47\n\nSource: NTSB Marine Accident Brief MAB-17/30 (public report). Animated illustration, not a reconstruction.\n\n#marineaccident #shipping #tanker #neworleans #mississippiriver #seafarer #merchantnavy #bridgeteam #NTSB #maritimesafety #jaimarineshorts",
